    "payload": {
      "answer": "Recorded in the ledger as a first-class relationship -- origin job id plus origin seq on the new job -- and surfaced two ways: in `vibey status` alongside the job, and in whatever the fork command prints on creation. Without lineage a forked run is indistinguishable from an unrelated one, which defeats the exploration case entirely: comparing two approaches requires knowing they share an origin. Provenance is not a nice-to-have here, it is the feature.",
      "item_id": "fork_lineage"
